# spec-review-proposal: Proposal review and refinement

Use for proposal review, design questions or requested changes before `plan-accept`. It grants no acceptance, merge or Development authority; the policy is the `spec` skill's [completion policy](../spec/references/completion.md#policy).

## Procedure

1. Read the proposal, every PADR and the envelopes at the current committed source SHA on `plan-<slug>`. Optionally run `devkit spec proposal report <slug> --source-sha <sha>` for a briefing or template.
2. Explain each decision's problem, choice, rejected alternatives and consequences, highlighting changed ones; name scope impacts, effort and support-role gaps, open decisions, waivers and unverified areas.
3. Before an edit, take exclusive ownership of the Planning worktree from the Host; never edit beside a running worker or reopen an accepted plan (use a follow-up proposal). Change `plan-<slug>` through `devkit workflow next --unit <proposal-dir>`, commit, and hand the head and ownership back.
   After merging the base into `plan-<slug>`, run `devkit rules fix <proposal-dir>` and commit its repairs: the merge can hand off or rename IDs that unchanged proposal files cite, and the merge commit's gate does not check them.
{% if execution.environment == "local" %}4. When readiness holds, present the findings, committed source and prospective effects to the user. Then run `devkit spec proposal accept <slug> --mode accept_only|accept_and_handoff --by user`, or run `devkit spec proposal handoff <slug> --effort low|medium|high` for an already accepted base. The Host carries conversational approval under `ask`. After a partial result, inspect actual Git and worktree state before retrying remaining effects.
{% else %}4. When readiness holds, return the committed source SHA and review findings to the Host. Only a separately authorized CLI/PR route records acceptance (`devkit spec proposal accept`) and hands off.
{% endif %}
## Completion

- The review is bound to the committed `plan-<slug>` head and presented to the user.
{% if execution.environment == "local" %}- Acceptance and handoff results report the CLI operation, selected effort and completed effects.
{% else %}- Nothing was accepted or handed off without separate authorization.
{% endif %}
